<title>FRANCE: EU postpones U.S. rice quota discussion - sources.</title>
<headline>EU postpones U.S. rice quota discussion - sources.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has postponed until next week discussion on a duty-free import quota of U.S. rice, to allow for fine-tuning of legal documents, grain industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>EU experts meeting on Thursday were also to focus on a &quot;cumulative recovery system&quot; for calculating duties on rice imports for the 1996/97 marketing year, they said.</p>
<p>The U.S. last week filed a complaint with the World Trade Organisation, saying that the EU's import tariff system for grains, including rice, infringed free-trade rules.</p>
</text>
